    "input": {
      "body": "Hi Caroleen,\n\nI previously asked which recurring document bottleneck you'd remove at CTA Law. This article takes a step back and looks at what makes an AI improvement last.\n\nThe main idea is that the team needs clear responsibilities and a shared review process, not just a faster drafting tool. That's shaping our approach to AI adoption at Possible Minds.\n\nhttps://getpossibleminds.com/t/XE55BYEdLg\n\nFrom your managing attorney's perspective, what seems harder: choosing the AI or changing how work moves through the team? I'd value a quick reply.\n\nBest,\nPranav\nFounder, Possible Minds",
      "subject": "Re: where AI could compound at CTA Law, APLC",
